Commissioning Guide for Hydroelectric Facilities — FIST 4-7 (@pe-fist-commission: 0, is #reference, #part-of @pe-sources) { r_0WA7RR86PMVEA3FFM7CG6NQ5RM
U.S. Bureau of Reclamation. Commissioning Guide for Hydroelectric Facilities, FIST 4-7, August 2023. [Official catalogue](https://www.usbr.gov/power/data/fist_pub.html) · [Complete guide](https://www.usbr.gov/power/data/fist/FIST_4-7_%288-2023%29.pdf).

Read the complete guide during a facility/commissioning investigation. Connect functional design, construction evidence, component tests, control/protection interfaces, system integration, operating conditions and transfer to maintenance. Compare a successful isolated component test with evidence that the complete system performs its intended function.

The official catalogue identifies the title/date; the 12,370,205-byte file exceeded automated inspection limits on 29 October 2026. Full-page inspection is not claimed. Hydro-specific and Reclamation requirements need interpretation when comparing another facility; do not transplant checklists as proof of suitability. Preserve actual revision and component notices. A reading guide cannot substitute for qualified commissioning experience, and an analysed published case must be labelled as documentary evidence. No manual or commissioning records are copied here.

**Return:** [Power-engineering sources — complete books, courses, methods and evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_12EFX00X7ZXGT9MPMJDYRTNY9N).
